# A module `local` that shadows one of the module's OWN top-level bindings —
# ouroboros#141, the case the issue's first comment said might need refusing
# by name (`lib/tensor.eigs`'s `scale`: a top-level function of that name plus
# `local scale is ...` inside two others; measured as 1 of 77 stdlib modules).
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that it needs NO refusal. The renamer moves the
# module's top-level bindings to `<M>__<name>` and its parameters / `for` /
# `try` / listcomp binders to `<M>__bnd__<name>`; module `local`s are
# deliberately NOT renamed, and are handled instead by the emitter's
# g_locshadow / g_boxshadow machinery, which block-scopes a numeric shadow to
# a C local (F-OURO-33) and gives a boxed one a per-call env binding
# (F-OURO-35). The two layers meet here: inside `use_local_fn` the name
# `depth` must reach the C block-local, NOT the renamed module function
# `_shadow_fn__depth` — and the program keeps its own `depth` and `factor`
# across the whole thing.
#
# Both shadow kinds are exercised: over a top-level FUNCTION (`depth`) and
# over a top-level NUMBER (`factor`). `use_global` then proves the module's
# own unshadowed reads still reach the renamed bindings.
depth is 1
factor is 2
import _shadow_fn
print of (_shadow_fn.use_local_fn of 4)
print of (_shadow_fn.use_local_num of 4)
print of (_shadow_fn.use_global of 5)
print of (_shadow_fn.depth of 6)
print of _shadow_fn.factor
print of depth
print of factor
